---
title: Use in Markdoc
description: Turn on Markdoc, add the pageMarkdoc() preset, and write RefineUI components as Markdoc tags.
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

Markdoc pages use tags instead of imports. `@pelagornis/page/markdoc` ships a preset that registers tags for the RefineUI components that render without client state. This page is an `.mdoc` file, so every example below is rendered by those tags.

## Install Markdoc

```sh
bun add @astrojs/markdoc @astrojs/starlight-markdoc
```

Add the Markdoc integration before Starlight.

```ts {% title="astro.config.ts" %}
import markdoc from "@astrojs/markdoc";
import starlight from "@astrojs/starlight";
import pagePlugin from "@pelagornis/page";
import { defineConfig } from "astro/config";

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    markdoc(),
    starlight({
      title: "My Docs",
      plugins: [pagePlugin()],
    }),
  ],
});
```

## Add the preset

Create `markdoc.config.mjs` next to the Astro config. `starlightMarkdoc()` brings Starlight's own tags such as `aside`. `pageMarkdoc()` adds the RefineUI tags.

```js {% title="markdoc.config.mjs" %}
import { defineMarkdocConfig } from "@astrojs/markdoc/config";
import starlightMarkdoc from "@astrojs/starlight-markdoc";
import pageMarkdoc from "@pelagornis/page/markdoc";

export default defineMarkdocConfig({
  extends: [starlightMarkdoc(), pageMarkdoc()],
});
```

## Write tags

Attributes use the React prop names and values. A tag with content needs a matching closing tag. A tag without content closes itself with a slash before the final `%}`.

```md {% process=false %}
{% stack direction="row" gap="sizeSmall" align="center" %}
{% badge variant="success" %}Stable{% /badge %}
{% button variant="primary" %}Continue{% /button %}
{% button variant="outline" %}Cancel{% /button %}
{% /stack %}
```

{% stack direction="row" gap="sizeSmall" align="center" class="not-content" %}
{% badge variant="success" %}Stable{% /badge %}
{% button variant="primary" %}Continue{% /button %}
{% button variant="outline" %}Cancel{% /button %}
{% /stack %}

Numbers and booleans are written without quotes.

```md {% process=false %}
{% progress value=60 ariaLabel="Upload" /%}
{% checkbox label="Send release emails" defaultChecked=true /%}
```

{% stack gap="sizeMedium" class="not-content" %}
{% progress value=60 ariaLabel="Upload" /%}
{% checkbox label="Send release emails" defaultChecked=true /%}
{% /stack %}

Use `ariaLabel` where the React prop is `aria-label`. Every tag also accepts `class` and `id`.

## Tags in the preset

| Tag | Component | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `box`, `container`, `grid`, `stack`, `spacer` | `Box`, `Container`, `Grid`, `Stack`, `Spacer` | Layout with token props |
| `divider` | `Divider` | Content becomes the inline label |
| `text` | `Text` | `variant` defaults to `bodyMd` |
| `button`, `link` | `Button`, `Link` | `link` requires `href` |
| `label`, `input`, `textarea`, `checkbox`, `radio` | Form controls | Native inputs, no client script |
| `badge`, `chip` | `Badge`, `Chip` | Content is the label |
| `progress`, `spinner`, `skeleton` | Feedback | `progress` requires `value` |
| `icon` | `WebIcon` | `name` is a RefineUI icon name |
| `avatars` | `Avatars` | `avatars=[{alt: "Name"}]` |

## Add a tag for an interactive component

Tags render Astro components on the server. A component with client state needs an `.astro` wrapper that hydrates it. Compose the component in a `.tsx` file as described in [Use in MDX](/guides/mdx/), then wrap it.

```astro {% title="src/components/markdoc/TabsExample.astro" %}
---
import TabsExample from "../TabsExample";
---

<TabsExample client:load />
```

Register the wrapper next to the preset.

```js {% title="markdoc.config.mjs" %}
import { component, defineMarkdocConfig } from "@astrojs/markdoc/config";
import starlightMarkdoc from "@astrojs/starlight-markdoc";
import pageMarkdoc from "@pelagornis/page/markdoc";

export default defineMarkdocConfig({
  extends: [starlightMarkdoc(), pageMarkdoc()],
  tags: {
    "tabs-example": {
      render: component("./src/components/markdoc/TabsExample.astro"),
      selfClosing: true,
    },
  },
});
```

```md {% process=false %}
{% tabs-example /%}
```

{% tabs-example /%}

Each [component page](/components/) lists the Markdoc tag for that component, or the wrapper to write when it needs one.
